## 2.7. In vitro antibacterial efficacy assay
The antibacterial efficacy was evaluated using Gram-positive S. aureus (ATCC 6538) and Gram-negative E. coli O157:H7 (ATCC 43895) as testing strains. The bacteria were cultured in Luria Broth (LB) medium at \(37\,^{\circ}\mathrm{C}\) overnight. The cultured bacteria were harvested and washed with PBS, then resuspended in PBS ( \(100\ \mathrm{mM}\), pH 7.4) with a final concentration of \(1\times10^{6}\) - \(\times\,10^{7}\,\mathrm{CFU/mL}\). The prepared bacterial suspensions were treated with groups of \(\mathrm{Cu@ZIF/GOx}\), \(\mathrm{GOx+}\) glucose, \(\mathrm{Cu@ZIF/GOx+}\) glucose, \(\mathrm{BC/GOx+}\) glucose and \(\mathrm{BC/GG-Cu@ZIF/GOx+}\) glucose under \(160~\mathrm{rpm}\) rotation at \(37\,^{\circ}\mathrm{C}\) for \(6\,\mathrm{h}\). The concentration of glucose, GOx, \(\mathrm{Cu@ZIF/GOx}\) and \(\mathrm{BC/GG}\) and \(\mathrm{BC/GG-Cu@ZIF/GOx}\) hydrogel are \(10\ \mathrm{mM}\), \(100~\upmu\mathrm{g/mL}\), \(100~\upmu\mathrm{g/mL}\) and \(200~\upmu\mathrm{L/mL}\) and \(200~\upmu\mathrm{L/mL}\), respectively. After incubation, the bacterial suspensions were diluted 10, 100, and 1000 times with PBS. The diluted bacterial suspensions were plated on the agar medium and incubated at \(37\,^{\circ}\mathrm{C}\) for 18 h. The bacteria colony was counted as \(\mathrm{CFU/mL}\).
For observing the bacteria adhesion and elimination effect of the prepared hydrogels, after incubating with bacterial suspensions, BC/GG and \(\mathrm{BC/GG-Cu@ZIF/GOx}\) hydrogels were taken out and rinsed with PBS, followed by immersing in \(2.5\%\) glutaraldehyde solution for \(2\,\mathrm{h}\). Then the hydrogels were dehydrated sequentially with gradient ethanol and dried at room temperature. SEM was carried out for observing the bacteria adhered on the hydrogels.
The biofilm eradication ability of the prepared samples was assessed using a crystal violet staining method as reported (Sun, Gao, Dong, Ren, & Qu, 2014). Briefly, to form biofilm, the cultured bacteria were harvested and resuspended in proper media with a concentration of \(1\times10^{7}\) \(\mathrm{CFU/mL}\) (Tryptone Soy Broth (TSB) media supplemented with \(0.5\%\) glucose for S. aureus and M9 medium supplemented with \(0.5\%\) glucose and \(0.4\%\) tryptone for E. coli). The bacteria suspensions were added in 24-well microtiter plates (1 mL each well) and incubated at \(37\,^{\circ}\mathrm{C}\) for 48 h. After incubation, the medium was discarded and each well was washed with PBS to remove unbound bacterial cells. The established biofilms were incubated with \(\mathrm{Cu@ZIF/GOx}\), \(\mathrm{GOx+}\) glucose, \(\mathrm{Cu@ZIF/GOx+}\) glucose, \(\mathrm{BC/GG+}\) glucose and \(\mathrm{BC/GG-Cu@ZIF/GOx+}\) glucose in biofilm minimal medium (TSB for S. aureus and M9 for E. coli) at \(37\,^{\circ}\mathrm{C}\) for \(12\,\mathrm{~h~}\). The concentration of GOx, \(\mathrm{Cu@ZIF/GOx}\), \(\mathrm{BC/GG}\), \(\mathrm{BC/GG-Cu@ZIF/GOx}\) and glucose in the medium are \(100~\upmu\mathrm{g/mL}\) and \(100~\upmu\mathrm{g/}\) mL, \(200~\upmu\mathrm{L/mL}\), \(200~\upmu\mathrm{L/mL}\) and \(0.1\,\mathrm{\wt\%}\), respectively. The biofilms incubated with minimal medium were used as control samples. After 12 h incubation, floating bacteria were washed out with PBS from each well and biofilms were stained with \(1\,\mathrm{mL}\) crystal violet stain (containing \(0.2\%\) crystal violet, \(1.9\%\) ethanol and \(0.08\%\) ammonium oxalate in PBS) for \(20\;\mathrm{min}\) in each well. The stained biofilms were rinsed with PBS for 3 times to remove the unbonded dye, the residual crystal violet stained biofilms were identified by solubilizing in \(100\%\) ethanol and measuring \(\mathrm{O.D.585nm}\).
## 2.8. In vitro cytocompatibility and hemolysis assay
NIH 3T3 cells were used as model cells for evaluating the cytocompatibility of the obtained materials. NIH 3T3 cells with the density of about 5000 cells/well in 96-well plates containing \(1\,\mathrm{mL}\) of Dulbecco's modified eagle medium (DMEM) were incubated at \(37\,^{\circ}\mathrm{C}\) for \(24\,\mathrm{h}\). After incubation, the medium was replaced with fresh medium containing \(0.1\,\mathrm{wt\%}\) glucose, and groups of 1) \(\mathrm{Cu@ZIF}\) \((100~\upmu\mathrm{g/mL})\), 2) \(\mathrm{Cu@ZIF/GOx}\) \((100~\upmu\mathrm{g/mL})\), 3) \(100~\upmu\mathrm{L}\) of \(\mathrm{BC/GG}\) hydrogel, and 4) \(100~\upmu\mathrm{L}\) of \(\mathrm{BC/GG-Cu@ZIF/GOx}\) hydrogel were added in the medium and incubated at \(37\,^{\circ}\mathrm{C}\) for \(24\,\mathrm{~h~}\). Medium without additives was used as control. Cells viability was quantified by 3-(4,5-dimethyl-2-thiazolyl)-2,5-diphenyl-2H-tetrazolium bromide (MTT) assay. Micrographs of cells were captured to observe the morphologies.
