In vitro hemolysis assay was performed following the described method (Cheng et al., 2020). The fresh rabbit blood with the addition of citrate-dextrose solution (9:1 in volume) as anticoagulant was centrifugated at \(3000~\mathrm{rpm}\) for \(10\ \mathrm{min}\) to collect erythrocytes and washed with PBS buffer. \(100~\upmu\mathrm{L}\) of the collected erythrocytes was added in \(5\,\mathrm{mL}\) PBS buffer and incubated with 1) \(100~\upmu\mathrm{g/mL}\) \(\mathrm{Cu@ZIF}\), 2) \(100~\upmu\mathrm{g/mL}\) \(\mathrm{Cu@ZIF/GOx}\), 3) \(500~\upmu\mathrm{L}\) BC/GG hydrogel, and 4) \(500~\upmu\mathrm{L}\) BC/GG-Cu@ZIF/GOx hydrogel. \(100~\upmu\mathrm{L}\) erythrocytes in \(5\,\mathrm{mL}\) PBS buffer and \(100~\upmu\mathrm{L}\) erythrocytes in \(5\,\mathrm{mL}\) distilled water were used as negative and positive controls, respectively. The samples were incubated at \(37\,^{\circ}\mathrm{C}\) for \(1\,\mathrm{h}\) and then centrifugated to obtain the supernatants. \(\mathrm{O.D.540\,\nm}\) of the supernatants was measured using a UV–vis spectrophotometer. Hemolysis rate was calculated according to the equation:
\[
\mathrm{Hemolysis~rate~}(\%)=[(\mathrm{A_s}-\mathrm{A_1})/(\mathrm{A_0}-\mathrm{A_1})]\times100
\]
where \(\mathbf{A}_{\mathrm{s}}\) is the absorbance of the samples, \(\mathbf{A}_{0}\) and \(\mathbf{A}_{1}\) are the absorbance of positive and negative controls, respectively.
