For mouse liver hemorrhage model test, the mouse liver was exposed by abdominal incision, pre-weighted filter paper with hydrophobic membrane on the back was placed beneath the liver to absorb the blood. Wound bleeding on the liver was created using a scalpel. A piece of BC/ GG-Cu@ZIF/GOx hydrogel was immediately covered on the bleeding site. After stopping the bleeding, the weight of the filter paper was measured for calculating blood mass. The bleeding liver without hydrogel was applied as control.
For mouse-tail amputation model test, pre-weighted filter paper was placed beneath the tail of anesthetized mouse, \(2\,\mathrm{cm}\) of the tail was cut off by a surgical scissors. After \(10\,\mathrm{~s~}\) , BC/GG-Cu@ZIF/GOx hydrogel was covered on the bleeding tail. After stopping the bleeding, the weight of the filter paper was measured and compared with control sample (without hydrogel).
